        <mxCell id="sOIr0pcRVrEv0dQ-mltz-106" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=25;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;This diagram shows the current AWS high-level architecture supporting a microservices platform across multiple accounts, highlighting inefficiencies in compute, storage, and scaling. The proposed architecture maintains the same structure but introduces targeted optimizations such as EC2 rightsizing, autoscaling, storage lifecycle management, and EKS optimization. The FinOps layer ensures continuous cost visibility, governance, and operational control.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
